---
import Layout from "@layouts/Layout.astro";
import Container from "@components/container.astro";
import Sectionhead from "@components/sectionhead.astro";

---

<Layout title="Projects">
  <Container>
    <Sectionhead>
      <Fragment slot="title">Projects</Fragment>
      <Fragment slot="desc">Some ideas deserve to be challenged, some problems just need fixing. A screen recorder that never phones home, a Mac that finally explains why it's slow, a card game that needs nothing but a phone, wisdom worth keeping, and numbers that are hard to look away from.</Fragment>
    </Sectionhead>

    <div class="flex flex-col gap-24 mx-auto max-w-6xl mt-16">
      
      {/* Reel */}
      <section class="grid grid-cols-12 gap-12">
        <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-6">
          <img 
            src="/Dave-Huntley/projects/Reel.png" 
            alt="The Reel site: a recording in progress with a camera bubble in the corner and a burned-in caption reading right, this is the bit I mentioned"
            class="rounded-lg shadow-lg w-full"
          />
        </div>
        
        <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-6">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">Reel</h2>
          <p class="text-xl text-slate-600 mb-6">Loom, without the account.</p>

          <p class="text-slate-700 mb-4">Every walkthrough you have ever recorded for a colleague is sitting on someone else's server, attached to a login, under a retention policy nobody read. Reel does the same job and never leaves the Mac: the screen, a camera bubble you drag wherever you like, your voice, and captions transcribed by the speech model macOS already ships. There is nothing to upload it to.</p>

          <p class="text-slate-700 mb-4">The part that took longest is the part you cannot see. Your microphone and the Mac's own output run on separate clocks that drift apart, so mixing them into the video as it records bakes in an error you can never take back out. It records picture and sound apart and joins them after you press stop, which is also why the raw audio and the uncaptioned cut stay on disk. Get a name wrong, fix the line, burn the captions again. <strong>Nobody has to say it twice.</strong></p>
          
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-8">
            <span class="bg-slate-100 px-3 py-1 rounded text-slate-700 text-sm">macOS</span>
            <span class="bg-slate-100 px-3 py-1 rounded text-slate-700 text-sm">Swift</span>
            <span class="bg-slate-100 px-3 py-1 rounded text-slate-700 text-sm">Screen Recording</span>
            <span class="bg-slate-100 px-3 py-1 rounded text-slate-700 text-sm">On-device AI</span>
          </div>

          <div class="flex gap-4 items-center">
            <a href="https://stimul8d.github.io/reel/" class="px-6 py-2.5 bg-slate-900 text-white hover:bg-slate-800 rounded-md transition-colors">View Live</a>
            <a href="https://github.com/stimul8d/reel" class="px-6 py-2.5 text-slate-600 hover:text-slate-900 transition-colors">Source →</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <hr class="border-slate-200" />

      {/* ProcWatch */}
      <section class="grid grid-cols-12 gap-12">
        <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-6">
          <img 
            src="/Dave-Huntley/projects/ProcWatch.png" 
            alt="The ProcWatch panel hanging from the macOS menu bar, flagging a Gradle daemon that has been at 187% for three minutes"
            class="rounded-lg shadow-lg w-full"
          />
        </div>
        
        <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-6">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">ProcWatch</h2>
          <p class="text-xl text-slate-600 mb-6">Why is your Mac slow?</p>

          <p class="text-slate-700 mb-4">Activity Monitor lists what's running. It doesn't tell you what's wrong. ProcWatch sits in the menu bar watching for the things that actually make a machine crawl: something flat out for minutes rather than seconds, memory pressure that won't let up, dev servers still holding ports days after the terminal closed.</p>

          <p class="text-slate-700 mb-4">The difference is that it waits. A compile is meant to peg a core, so it gets three minutes before anyone hears about it. A language server gets forty-five seconds. And it names things properly: not <span class="font-mono text-sm">node</span>, but the dev server, which project it belongs to and which port it's sat on. Then it kills the whole tree, including the children npm leaves behind.</p>
          
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-8">
            <span class="bg-slate-100 px-3 py-1 rounded text-slate-700 text-sm">macOS</span>
            <span class="bg-slate-100 px-3 py-1 rounded text-slate-700 text-sm">Swift</span>
            <span class="bg-slate-100 px-3 py-1 rounded text-slate-700 text-sm">Developer Tools</span>
            <span class="bg-slate-100 px-3 py-1 rounded text-slate-700 text-sm">Menu Bar</span>
          </div>

          <div class="flex gap-4 items-center">
            <a href="https://stimul8d.github.io/procwatch/" class="px-6 py-2.5 bg-slate-900 text-white hover:bg-slate-800 rounded-md transition-colors">View Live</a>
            <a href="https://github.com/stimul8d/procwatch" class="px-6 py-2.5 text-slate-600 hover:text-slate-900 transition-colors">Source →</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <hr class="border-slate-200" />

      {/* Cards */}
      <section class="grid grid-cols-12 gap-12">
        <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-6">
          <img 
            src="/Dave-Huntley/projects/Cards.png" 
            alt="The Cards join screen: a name field, a button to start a new game, and a room code box"
            class="rounded-lg shadow-lg w-full"
          />
        </div>
        
        <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-6">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">Cards</h2>
          <p class="text-xl text-slate-600 mb-6">A terrible game for terrible friends</p>

          <p class="text-slate-700 mb-4">Cards Against Humanity without the box. One person starts a game and reads the room code out, everyone else joins from whatever phone is already in their hand. No accounts, no app to install, nothing to pass around the table.</p>

          <p class="text-slate-700 mb-4">Card content comes from the official sets, released by their authors under CC BY-NC-SA, plus the community packs. Not affiliated with Cards Against Humanity LLC, and no relation to the several apps that want your email address before they'll let you play.</p>
          
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-8">
            <span class="bg-slate-100 px-3 py-1 rounded text-slate-700 text-sm">Party Game</span>
            <span class="bg-slate-100 px-3 py-1 rounded text-slate-700 text-sm">Multiplayer</span>
            <span class="bg-slate-100 px-3 py-1 rounded text-slate-700 text-sm">Room Codes</span>
            <span class="bg-slate-100 px-3 py-1 rounded text-slate-700 text-sm">Mobile First</span>
          </div>

          <div class="flex gap-4 items-center">
            <a href="https://github.com/stimul8d/cards" class="px-6 py-2.5 bg-slate-900 text-white hover:bg-slate-800 rounded-md transition-colors">Source →</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <hr class="border-slate-200" />

      {/* OpenMind */}
      <section class="grid grid-cols-12 gap-12">
        <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-6">
          <img 
            src="/Dave-Huntley/projects/OpenMind.png" 
            alt="OpenMind interface showing a philosophical quote with floating geometric shapes"
            class="rounded-lg shadow-lg w-full"
          />
        </div>
        
        <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-6">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">OpenMind</h2>
          <p class="text-xl text-slate-600 mb-6">A better class of wisdom</p>

          <p class="text-slate-700 mb-4">Look past the Instagram philosophers and motivational posters. OpenMind collects insights that have actually been tested - from survival stories to indigenous knowledge. Each quote comes with proper context about why it matters and how it's been proven to work.</p>
          
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-8">
            <span class="bg-slate-100 px-3 py-1 rounded text-slate-700 text-sm">Mental Models</span>
            <span class="bg-slate-100 px-3 py-1 rounded text-slate-700 text-sm">Indigenous Wisdom</span>
            <span class="bg-slate-100 px-3 py-1 rounded text-slate-700 text-sm">Survival Stories</span>
            <span class="bg-slate-100 px-3 py-1 rounded text-slate-700 text-sm">Sport Psychology</span>
          </div>

          <div class="flex gap-4 items-center">
            <a href="https://stimul8d.github.io/OpenMind/" class="px-6 py-2.5 bg-slate-900 text-white hover:bg-slate-800 rounded-md transition-colors">View Live</a>
            <a href="https://github.com/stimul8d/OpenMind" class="px-6 py-2.5 text-slate-600 hover:text-slate-900 transition-colors">Source →</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <hr class="border-slate-200" />

      {/* Kill Clock */}
      <section class="grid grid-cols-12 gap-12">
        <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-6">
          <img 
            src="/Dave-Huntley/projects/KillClock.png" 
            alt="Animal Kill Clock dashboard showing real-time statistics"
            class="rounded-lg shadow-lg w-full"
          />
        </div>
        
        <div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-6">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">Animal Kill Clock</h2>
          <p class="text-xl text-slate-600 mb-6">Making the invisible visible</p>

          <p class="text-slate-700 mb-4">Sometimes numbers tell the story better than words ever could. This real-time counter shows the true scale of animal agriculture, built specifically for street demonstrations and public events. Works offline, adapts to any screen size, and hits hard with pure data.</p>
          
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-8">
            <span class="bg-slate-100 px-3 py-1 rounded text-slate-700 text-sm">Animal Rights</span>
            <span class="bg-slate-100 px-3 py-1 rounded text-slate-700 text-sm">Data Visualisation</span>
            <span class="bg-slate-100 px-3 py-1 rounded text-slate-700 text-sm">Activism</span>
            <span class="bg-slate-100 px-3 py-1 rounded text-slate-700 text-sm">PWA</span>
          </div>

          <div class="flex gap-4 items-center">
            <a href="https://stimul8d.github.io/ARA-Kill-Clock/" class="px-6 py-2.5 bg-slate-900 text-white hover:bg-slate-800 rounded-md transition-colors">View Live</a>
            <a href="https://github.com/stimul8d/ARA-Kill-Clock" class="px-6 py-2.5 text-slate-600 hover:text-slate-900 transition-colors">Source →</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
      
    </div>
  </Container>
</Layout>